## Quality Check Rules

**All quality verification is done locally. CI is for build confirmation only.**

### Flow

```
Harness-only diff? -> skip quality-check entirely (the gate exempts it;
                      gate-parameter changes are NOT exempt - see Quality Check Hook)
    |
Step 1: Change area + risk level detection (git diff; risk levels per quality policy §1)
    |
Step 2/3: Static checks + tests (High/Medium: cross-check the test-design memo)
    |
Step 3.5: Mutation testing on the changed diff (High/Medium risk only; skipped when not configured)
    |
Step 4: Review cycles (staged personas by diff size, min 1 cycle; the QA persona works
        falsification-first - hunt for inputs that prove the implementation wrong;
        repeat only on High/Medium findings)
    |
Step 5: E2E tests (final verification)
    |
Step 6: Report data saved -> .quality-check-passed (commit-bound JSON) created -> merge allowed
```

Thresholds, cycle caps and time budgets are defined in `documents/development/quality-policy.md` (§1 risk levels, §2 gate matrix, §5 loop protection). Do not restate the numbers here - read them from the policy.

### Quality Check Hook

Codex enforces this via a `PreToolUse` hook (configured in `.codex/hooks.json`).
When you run `gh pr merge`, `git merge` on main, or push to main, Codex validates `.quality-check-passed` (commit-bound JSON: `{branch, commit}`). **Pushes to feature branches are not gated.** The flag is not consumed; it stays valid while post-check commits touch only harness files (`CLAUDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `.cursorrules`, `.claude/**`, `.codex/**`, `.cursor/**`, `skills/project/**`, `skills/superpowers/**`, `.github/review-*.md`, `documents/development/coding-rules/**`). Harness-only diffs skip the gate and the quality check entirely. **Carve-out**: a diff that changes gate parameters - the `Quality Gate Overrides` keys below - is NOT exempt, even inside those paths. It must go through quality-check (a reduced-persona review at minimum). If main advanced independently after the flag was issued, the merged main is unverified - re-run quality-check on it before pushing.

